{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1491838694,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEwMzY3MDQ3NjI="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1491973266,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5MzQ3NDUxMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-293474513"},"message":"Any thoughts on this @yarikoptic ?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1491995954,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5MzU0NzIzMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-293547231"},"message":"In general I like the idea... Yet to read few more times for better diggestion","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1492008416,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5MzYwMDk4Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-293600986"},"message":"that is what was nagging me:  such templates couldn't be \"composed\" together and thus would be not as flexible as they could be made if created on the fly given a set of specifications.  E.g. a particular case you brought up \n- \"`code/` folder in each dataset, and I always want to have all files in this directory to be committed to git directly and not annexed\".  \nAlthough indeed could be \"hard coded\" within few templates, it is a generic pattern which could be useful for many other datasets and as such ideally should be just a feature you demand from a new dataset.\nThis reflects on old RFC #921 and #925 where we tried to discuss how we could simplify/standardize some \"features\" we are assigning to created siblings or new datasets.  So it feels to me that we might better come up with a list of dataset/sibling \"features\" (which are just a set of tags we understand) which trigger specific actions. E.g.\n- `with-code` \n   - would be your usecase which would trigger action \"modify .gitattributes to instruct annex to commit `code/` straight under git\"\n- `bids`:\n   - adds/processes `with-code` feature\n   - expand .gitattributes to instruct to add top-level README, *tsv etc directly to git\n   - (not sure if possible actually but ...) set `.gitattributes` to instruct to add `distribution-restrictions` for `sourcedata/` content upon their commit.  Or at least, if operating on top of existing but not yet in datalad directory -- do corresponding `git-annex metadata` call\n   - trigger `datalad metadata-edit --type=bids` (#1457) to establish `dataset_description.json`\n   - initiate README (although may be should be done by above step)\n   - I am not sure what else could be in \"BIDS skeleton\" (even subject IDs are nohow regimented) but that is only the level where I think some tarball template might be appropriate to consider -- just to compliment with some files layout but again as triggered by this \"feature\" which would do other actions\n- `nodata`, `public`, `alltags`, `allbranches` (#925)\n   - would tune up git annex wanted and git/config on what that dataset/sibling should contain\n- `crawl`:\n   - would trigger `crawl-init` in some kind of interactive mode\n\nand may be even allow to be of the form `name=value` so we could add/pass options into corresponding actions. And then may be even allow for that simple templating from a tarball but without much on top...\n\nE.g. examples\n- `datalad create --features=with-code` - your original use case\n- `datalad create --features=template=/path/mylab.tar.gz`\n  - to initiate from some template, and if `metadata` type is set within its dataset config, issue `metadata-edit`  with its type\n- `datalad create --features=bids:license=CC,crawl:template=openfmri`\n   - in this case `license=CC` becomes an option within `datalad edit-metadata --type=bids --license=CC` call\n- `datalad create-sibling --features=unique-data,public,alltags,allbranches`\n   - to create a sibling to publish derivative data publicly (thus imposing restriction to not publish data with restrictions)\n\nSo altogether it feels that we could benefit from \"template tarballs\" but imho it should be just an additional feature within a more generic approach","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1492010138,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5MzYxMDQ5Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-293610493"},"message":"I like that in general. However, I see these as two related, but different things.\n\n\u003e that is what was nagging me: such templates couldn't be \"composed\" together\n\nWhy not? Multiple template tarballs superimposed on each other. What is most important to me is that there is a mechanism that allows me to compose datasets with a custom structure that does not need to have been envisioned by datalad authors.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1492013671,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5MzYyOTczMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-293629731"},"message":"\u003e Multiple template tarballs superimposed on each other. \n\nand what to happen if both tarballs provide `.gitattributes`?  I could only see approach similar to what I do in crawler:  create detached branches for both tarballs, extract, and then do 'git merge' them into a single piece.\n\n\u003e compose datasets with a custom structure that does not need to have been envisioned by datalad authors\n\nyou (i.e. any user) could always do that without anything special in datalad. `cp` or `rsync` your favorite template one before you call `datalad create --force` within the copy ;)  but indeed **us** providing some templates would be handy (as we envision them)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1493394693,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5ODAzNTI3Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-298035272"},"message":"just for the record, had to come up with this .gitattributes:\n```\n* annex.backend=MD5E\n# top level text files -- git\n* annex.largefiles=(not(mimetype=text/*))\n# everything underneath subdirectories -- annex\n**/* annex.largefiles=anything\n```\nedit: actually above one is \"wrong\" -- not sure how it worked when I have tried since then it didn't work correctly later... correct one seems to be\n```\n* annex.backend=MD5E\n# everything underneath subdirectories -- annex\n* annex.largefiles=anything\n# top level text files -- git\n/* annex.largefiles=(not(mimetype=text/*))\n```\nconfirmation for my sanity:\n```shell\n$\u003e git check-attr --all 1 bu/1 bu/du/1          \n1: annex.backend: MD5E\n1: annex.largefiles: (not(mimetype=text/*))\nbu/1: annex.backend: MD5E\nbu/1: annex.largefiles: anything\nbu/du/1: annex.backend: MD5E\nbu/du/1: annex.largefiles: anything\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1493408434,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5ODA4OTAwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-298089005"},"message":"damn I want this feature in some reincarnation now :-/  becomes really needed for automated crawling of collections with bunch of sub-repos... e.g. if I know that they all will be BIDS datasets I would want to instruct that subdatasets should be creating following some template which in turn would provide correct values in .gitattributes one way or another","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1498455347,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxMDk2Nzc1MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-310967751"},"message":"Work towards this is happening in #1619","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1498455354,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDExMzgwNTM3NzU="},"added":["do-as-extension"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1509262540,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM0MDI0MzMzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-340243333"},"message":"FTR: @bpoldrack language to setup test repos is already capable enough to do most of this. We should use it for this purpose too, and not have yet another solution.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1509542933,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM0MTEwNTk5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-341105996"},"message":"Agree. Need to RF to extract that layer of interpreting that \"language\" and use it for templates again. Probably just needs some additional string mappings.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528799182,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5NjU0MjMyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1462#issuecomment-396542325"},"message":"We have `run-procedure` now that can run scripts that set up datasets in any way.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1528799182,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTY3NTkzMDY2OQ=="},"status":2}]}